<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tajiks</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tajiks are a Persian-speaking people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, living mainly in Tajikistan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>. They descend largely from the Iranian population of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bactria">Bactria</a> and Sogdiana, and cities such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a> were centres of their culture. The Soviet borders drawn in the 1920s left many Tajiks outside the Tajik republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tajiks.jpg" alt="Tajiks" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ilhoms · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Happy_Tajik_children.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
